WEBVTT

00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:02.395
Here's the curve y equals e to the

00:00:02.556 --> 00:00:02.596
x.

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:06.013
Squash it sideways, and you get y equals

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.258
e to the two x.

00:00:08.062 --> 00:00:10.009
Or slide it one unit left, and you

00:00:10.029 --> 00:00:12.058
get y equals e to the x plus

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:12.298
one.

00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:14.607
At x equals zero,

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:17.779
which new curve do you think is steeper?

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.316
Hold on to your guess.

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:20.552
Here's the twist.

00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:23.247
Only one of them puts a new factor

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:25.296
into its derivative, and it might not be

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:25.999
the one you'd pick.

00:00:26.661 --> 00:00:29.209
By the end, you'll know why, and how

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.137
to differentiate k e to the a x

00:00:32.177 --> 00:00:32.679
plus b.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.261
Two quick reminders.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.912
The gradient at a point is the slope

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:39.399
of the tangent there, the line the secants

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.645
settle onto as the second point slides in.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.260
And e to the x is its own

00:00:44.302 --> 00:00:44.784
derivative.

00:00:45.388 --> 00:00:47.475
On the graph, that means at every point,

00:00:47.596 --> 00:00:50.225
the gradient equals the height, the y value.

00:00:50.928 --> 00:00:53.618
Where the curve is one unit high, the

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:55.264
tangent's slope is one.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.719
Where it's about two point seven high, the

00:00:58.761 --> 00:01:00.065
slope is about two point seven.

00:01:00.669 --> 00:01:02.697
Height and gradient always match,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.264
and that's our measuring stick.

00:01:05.104 --> 00:01:06.036
Now squash it.

00:01:06.681 --> 00:01:08.809
In e to the two x, x gets

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.098
doubled before the exponential acts.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:14.792
So the new curve reaches every height in

00:01:14.993 --> 00:01:16.379
half the sideways distance.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.857
Watch this tangent triangle.

00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:22.454
It runs across one unit and rises about

00:01:22.595 --> 00:01:23.378
two point seven.

00:01:24.122 --> 00:01:26.837
Squash the curve, and the triangle squashes with

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:26.938
it.

00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:29.894
The rise stays the same, but the run

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:30.738
halves.

00:01:31.462 --> 00:01:34.134
Same rise, half the run, so the slope

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.138
is twice as steep.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:38.835
The whole curve squashed evenly, so that's true

00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:39.518
at every point.

00:01:40.202 --> 00:01:41.995
At height one, the slope is now two.

00:01:42.841 --> 00:01:45.367
The gradient is always two times the height,

00:01:45.788 --> 00:01:47.593
so the derivative of e to the two

00:01:47.753 --> 00:01:49.738
x is two e to the two x.

00:01:50.748 --> 00:01:53.415
Squash by three, and every run shrinks to

00:01:53.456 --> 00:01:56.304
a third, so every slope is three times

00:01:56.325 --> 00:01:56.765
as steep.

00:01:57.408 --> 00:01:59.476
The derivative of e to the three x

00:01:59.758 --> 00:02:01.444
is three e to the three x.

00:02:02.108 --> 00:02:04.979
What about a negative number, like e to

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.144
the minus two x?

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.955
The minus also flips the curve in the

00:02:09.177 --> 00:02:11.545
y axis, so it falls instead of rising.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:15.642
Every uphill tangent becomes a downhill one, just

00:02:15.703 --> 00:02:16.044
as steep.

00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:19.342
So the gradient is minus two times the

00:02:19.383 --> 00:02:19.583
height.

00:02:20.409 --> 00:02:23.501
The height stays positive, because e to any

00:02:23.562 --> 00:02:24.565
power is positive.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.923
It's only the slope that turns negative.

00:02:27.584 --> 00:02:28.598
Now the slide.

00:02:29.121 --> 00:02:31.129
E to the x plus one is the

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.318
same curve moved one unit left.

00:02:34.163 --> 00:02:35.696
Sliding doesn't tilt anything.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.873
Each tangent just slides along with its point,

00:02:39.235 --> 00:02:39.939
keeping its slope.

00:02:40.561 --> 00:02:42.266
So the gradient still equals the height,

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.271
and the derivative of e to the x

00:02:44.291 --> 00:02:46.437
plus one is just e to the x

00:02:46.457 --> 00:02:46.939
plus one.

00:02:47.644 --> 00:02:48.354
Back to your guess.

00:02:49.141 --> 00:02:51.648
At x equals zero, the slid curve is

00:02:51.708 --> 00:02:54.516
about two point seven high, so its slope

00:02:54.596 --> 00:02:55.619
is about two point seven.

00:02:56.422 --> 00:02:58.854
The squashed curve is only one high there,

00:02:59.095 --> 00:02:59.859
with a slope of two.

00:03:00.482 --> 00:03:02.792
So the slid curve is steeper at zero

00:03:03.094 --> 00:03:04.138
only because it's higher.

00:03:04.822 --> 00:03:07.396
What matters is how the gradient compares with

00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:07.818
the height.

00:03:08.482 --> 00:03:10.757
Last change: stretch the curve upwards.

00:03:11.562 --> 00:03:13.812
Three e to the x makes every height

00:03:14.013 --> 00:03:15.058
three times taller.

00:03:15.843 --> 00:03:17.516
Look at the tangent triangle.

00:03:18.361 --> 00:03:21.510
The run doesn't change, but the rise is

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:22.653
three times bigger,

00:03:23.154 --> 00:03:24.979
so the slope is three times steeper.

00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:28.353
That's the Year 11 constant multiple rule: the

00:03:28.393 --> 00:03:29.699
three comes along for the ride.

00:03:30.261 --> 00:03:32.569
And notice, the gradient still equals the height,

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.978
because both grew by the same factor of

00:03:35.058 --> 00:03:35.299
three.

00:03:35.941 --> 00:03:38.672
So k scales everything, but only a changes

00:03:38.692 --> 00:03:40.178
the gradient compared with the height.

00:03:40.708 --> 00:03:42.940
Now let's prove it, with the Year 11

00:03:43.042 --> 00:03:43.564
chain rule.

00:03:44.168 --> 00:03:46.681
Take y equals e to the a x

00:03:46.822 --> 00:03:47.324
plus b.

00:03:48.028 --> 00:03:49.573
Call the inside part u,

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.685
so u equals a x plus b.

00:03:53.368 --> 00:03:53.627
Then y

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.332
equals e to the u,

00:03:55.975 --> 00:03:57.397
and since that's its own derivative,

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.864
d y by d u is e to

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:00.145
the u.

00:04:00.988 --> 00:04:03.335
The inside part's derivative, d u by d

00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:05.603
x, is just a, because the b is

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:06.145
a constant.

00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:08.294
The chain rule multiplies them:

00:04:08.978 --> 00:04:10.383
e to the u, times a.

00:04:11.328 --> 00:04:13.335
Put the inside part back, and you get

00:04:13.657 --> 00:04:15.824
a e to the a x plus b.

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:18.495
The b stays in the power, but it

00:04:18.596 --> 00:04:19.820
adds nothing to the factor,

00:04:20.383 --> 00:04:21.145
just like the slide.

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:23.900
And with k out the front, k just

00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:24.544
rides along.

00:04:25.104 --> 00:04:25.694
Let's use it.

00:04:26.301 --> 00:04:29.133
Differentiate y equals e to the three x.

00:04:31.261 --> 00:04:33.893
The inside part is three x, and its

00:04:33.953 --> 00:04:35.058
derivative is three.

00:04:35.721 --> 00:04:38.050
So keep e to the three x exactly

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:38.512
as it is,

00:04:39.114 --> 00:04:40.439
and multiply by three.

00:04:40.981 --> 00:04:43.856
The derivative is three e to the three

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:44.158
x.

00:04:44.924 --> 00:04:45.714
Check it on the graph.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.808
At x equals zero, the curve is one

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:51.837
unit high, and its slope is three, three

00:04:51.877 --> 00:04:52.499
times the height.

00:04:53.327 --> 00:04:53.895
One trap.

00:04:54.582 --> 00:04:56.212
Don't bring the power down like you would

00:04:56.292 --> 00:04:57.198
for x cubed.

00:04:57.761 --> 00:04:59.687
That rule needs x in the base, and

00:04:59.747 --> 00:05:00.008
here

00:05:00.529 --> 00:05:02.816
x is in the power, so the exponential

00:05:02.997 --> 00:05:03.619
stays whole.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:05.622
Now all three constants.

00:05:06.308 --> 00:05:06.790
The task:

00:05:07.314 --> 00:05:09.585
find f prime of minus three.

00:05:10.188 --> 00:05:13.098
The function is f of x equals five

00:05:13.299 --> 00:05:15.085
e to the two x plus six.

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:17.173
So k is five,

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:18.739
a is two and

00:05:19.523 --> 00:05:20.205
b is six.

00:05:20.748 --> 00:05:23.862
Copy the exponential, then multiply by k and

00:05:24.064 --> 00:05:24.204
a.

00:05:24.988 --> 00:05:27.575
Five times two is ten, so f prime

00:05:27.616 --> 00:05:29.782
of x is ten e to the two

00:05:29.904 --> 00:05:30.464
x plus six.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:32.882
Now substitute minus three.

00:05:33.548 --> 00:05:36.637
Two times minus three, plus six, is zero,

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.342
and e to the zero is one.

00:05:39.769 --> 00:05:41.961
So f prime of minus three is ten.

00:05:43.068 --> 00:05:45.894
On the graph, it's five high there with

00:05:45.935 --> 00:05:48.541
a slope of ten, twice the height, as

00:05:48.822 --> 00:05:50.365
a equals two predicts.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.383
Here's one way to remember it.

00:05:52.988 --> 00:05:55.216
Think of the power, a x plus b,

00:05:55.739 --> 00:05:57.305
as the playback speed of the curve.

00:05:58.072 --> 00:05:58.981
a is the speed.

00:05:59.728 --> 00:06:02.156
Play it twice as fast, and the curve

00:06:02.217 --> 00:06:04.364
rises twice as fast at every height.

00:06:05.109 --> 00:06:07.484
Play it backwards, and it falls instead.

00:06:08.108 --> 00:06:10.055
b just starts the playback at a different

00:06:10.116 --> 00:06:12.324
point, so it adds no rate factor.

00:06:13.048 --> 00:06:15.717
And k makes the whole picture bigger, so

00:06:15.818 --> 00:06:17.764
heights and slopes grow together.

00:06:18.468 --> 00:06:18.909
In short,

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:22.743
copy the exponential, then multiply by k and

00:06:22.844 --> 00:06:23.264
by a.

00:06:26.121 --> 00:06:26.527
Your turn.

00:06:27.155 --> 00:06:30.121
Differentiate f of x equals four e to

00:06:30.162 --> 00:06:32.748
the two x minus one, then find f

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.131
prime of a half.

00:06:35.137 --> 00:06:36.248
Pause here to answer.

00:06:46.961 --> 00:06:49.291
The inside part is two x minus one,

00:06:49.753 --> 00:06:51.039
with derivative two.

00:06:51.721 --> 00:06:51.941
So f

00:06:52.623 --> 00:06:55.269
prime of x is four times two, e

00:06:55.811 --> 00:06:57.675
to the two x minus one, which is

00:06:57.836 --> 00:06:59.319
eight e to the two x minus one.

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:01.987
At a half, the power is zero, and

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:04.073
e to the zero is one, so f

00:07:04.114 --> 00:07:05.819
prime of a half is eight.

00:07:06.602 --> 00:07:08.813
If you got four, you dropped the factor

00:07:08.833 --> 00:07:09.858
of two from the inside.

00:07:11.714 --> 00:07:12.261
Last one.

00:07:12.948 --> 00:07:16.060
A curve has equation y equals three e

00:07:16.141 --> 00:07:17.184
to the minus two x.

00:07:17.928 --> 00:07:20.314
Find its gradient at x equals zero,

00:07:20.937 --> 00:07:23.283
and explain why the curve is decreasing for

00:07:23.464 --> 00:07:23.945
every x.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:25.921
Pause here to answer.

00:07:36.721 --> 00:07:39.227
The derivative is three times minus two, e

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:42.234
to the minus two x, which is minus

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:44.059
six e to the minus two x.

00:07:44.842 --> 00:07:46.737
At zero, that's minus six.

00:07:47.481 --> 00:07:49.627
E to any power is positive, so e

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:52.034
to the minus two x is always positive.

00:07:52.716 --> 00:07:55.520
Times minus six, the gradient is negative for

00:07:55.721 --> 00:07:58.324
every x, so the curve is always decreasing.

00:07:59.108 --> 00:08:00.944
It isn't because the curve dips below zero.

00:08:01.448 --> 00:08:02.015
It never does.

00:08:03.728 --> 00:08:06.833
So horizontal scaling multiplies slopes by a,

00:08:07.395 --> 00:08:08.877
a slide adds no factor,

00:08:09.379 --> 00:08:11.703
and k multiplies heights and slopes.

00:08:12.588 --> 00:08:14.536
Next: what about two to the x?

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.526
Two to the x is secretly e to

00:08:17.587 --> 00:08:18.890
some number times x.

00:08:19.854 --> 00:08:22.122
Find that number, and you can differentiate it

00:08:22.164 --> 00:08:22.685
the same way.

00:08:25.295 --> 00:08:26.158
Here are the key notes.

00:08:26.561 --> 00:08:28.108
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:28.611
to copy them.
